# Accepted exceptions of the quality review (@softure-ai/quality-review, README "Accepted exceptions").
# One entry per line: a finding id, `rule <rule> <glob>` or `path <glob>`; `#` starts a comment.

# theme-flat-paint's react peer: the theme package contract (themes/theme-kit/README.md) has every theme take react
# as a peer, so an app moves between themes without changing its dependencies (issue #1287).
QR-60a7a98b

# auth registration answers auth.email_taken: registration signs the person in at once, with no email verification,
# so it cannot answer "check your inbox" for a taken address. A known limitation (modules/auth/README.md,
# Limitations), bounded by the `register` rate limit; login and password reset still hide accounts.
QR-5cebc6e2

# mcp-access token endpoint looks the client up before it counts: counting by address alone first would throttle an
# assistant platform that refreshes all its users' tokens from a few shared addresses. The lookup is one indexed read
# (ids over 255 characters run none), the cost of the counter itself; adopted clients keep their own id format, so a
# shape check cannot replace it (comment in handleTokenRequest).
QR-cc3a4799

# security subjectKey stores an unsalted SHA-256 prefix: keying it with an HMAC needs a server secret at every caller
# (auth, files, waitlist, billing, privacy), none of which has a context where it calls subjectKey. Rate limit rows
# live two windows, and README §11 states the keys are pseudonymous, not anonymous.
QR-bcbad772
